    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen a terminal notifies nvim of color mode change, nvim updates `background` option and reloads the color scheme, but it does not emit `OptionSet` or `ColorScheme` events.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- have this in init.lua\n```lua\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('OptionSet', {\n  pattern = 'background',\n  callback = function() print('background changed') end,\n}\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('ColorScheme', {\n  callback = function() print('color scheme changed') end,\n}\n```\n- start nvim in a terminal that tracks system color mode\n- change system color mode\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nEvents should be emitted, since `background` option was updated.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-nightly+f8872bc\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nnot sure\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nNixOS 26.11\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.48.2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\nNix flake (https://github.com/nix-community/neovim-nightly-overlay)",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
